ffuf (Fuzz Faster U Fool) is a fast web fuzzer written in Go. It is designed
for discovering hidden resources and testing web applications by fuzzing URLs,
HTTP headers, parameters, and POST data.

ffuf supports directory and file discovery, virtual host discovery, parameter
fuzzing, recursive scanning, multiple wordlists, response matching and
filtering, configurable request rates, and several output formats.

It can be used for web application security testing, penetration testing, and
content discovery on authorized targets.
